{"findings":[{"title":"[P1] Enforce operator authorization outside caller-controlled arguments","body":"The operator check trusts `--recorded-by decisions-command`, which any agent invoking the shell script can supply. `disable-model-invocation` restricts the slash command but does not protect direct script execution. An agent can call `context --clear --recorded-by decisions-command` to remove the unattended marker, then, when no other live-run signal holds, call `confirm --id DEC-0007 --recorded-by decisions-command --evidence cli:<timestamp> --answer-ref cli:<timestamp>` to approve its own proposal with operator attribution. The same spoofed identity authorizes rejection and supersession of decided rows. Enforce these transitions through an operator authorization mechanism unavailable to agent shell calls.","severity":"HIGH","category":"authz","confidence_score":0.99,"anchor":".claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh:op_context","anchor_type":"function","anchor_line":716,"anchor_line_end":718,"code_location":{"absolute_file_path":"/home/evaluser/.cache/loa/loa-codex-ws-jh1ld7u3/.claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh","line_range":{"start":716,"end":718}},"id":"DISS-001","description":"The operator check trusts caller-controlled `--recorded-by decisions-command` arguments, allowing agents invoking the shell script directly to clear the unattended marker and approve, reject, or supersede decisions with spoofed operator attribution.","id_derived":true,"failure_mode":"The operator check trusts caller-controlled `--recorded-by decisions-command` arguments, allowing agents invoking the shell script directly to clear the unattended marker and approve, reject, or super","failure_mode_derived":true,"anchor_status":"valid","anchor_stability":"symbol","voice":"gpt-5.5-pro","answered_by":"codex-headless"},{"id":"DISS-C-001","severity":"HIGH","category":"authz","anchor":".claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh:is_operator_call","anchor_type":"line","anchor_line":359,"anchor_line_end":359,"scope":"cross_file","trigger_anchor":".claude/commands/decisions.md","cross_file_justification":"decisions.md and .claude/data/user-invoked-commands.txt describe confirm, reject/supersede on decided rows and context --clear as operator-only because of disable-model-invocation. The runtime check in dec-write-lib.sh is only a comparison of a caller-supplied flag value, so the documented boundary is not enforced by the script.","description":"The operator-only gate is a string comparison of the --recorded-by flag against the constant decisions-command. Any caller with shell access can pass that flag. disable-model-invocation only stops the model from starting the /decisions slash command through the Skill tool; it does not stop a session from executing the writer script directly, and the slash command body itself tells the session to run that script. Attribution is derived from caller input too: op_confirm (line 538) sets decided_by to operator whenever decided_by_ref matches the OPREF_RE prefixes, and the cli:<iso-8601> form needs no artifact. The only additional gate, live_run_signal, is removed by the same unenforced flag via context --clear, or is simply absent in an interactive session. The bats test cited in decisions.md is a static scan of prompt files, not a runtime control.","failure_mode":"An agent, including one steered by prompt-injected ledger text, confirms rows it proposed itself, records them as decided by the operator, and the ledger that the SDD/PRD templates render as the operator's decisions no longer reflects operator review.","suggested_fix":"Do not treat --recorded-by as an authorization signal. Options, in order of strength: require an interactive terminal and a confirmation read from /dev/tty inside the script for confirm/clear; move the confirm transition out of the agent's reach (for example a separately-permissioned tool or a signed-commit check in CI that rejects proposed->decided transitions not made by the operator); at minimum add a Bash deny rule in .claude/settings.json for the writer's confirm/clear subcommands and reword decisions.md so it does not claim the model cannot invoke these operations.","anchor_status":"valid","anchor_stability":"symbol","voice":"claude-headless","answered_by":"claude-headless"},{"id":"DISS-C-002","severity":"MEDIUM","category":"input-validation","anchor":".claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh:op_import","anchor_type":"hunk","anchor_line":642,"anchor_line_end":647,"scope":"diff","trigger_anchor":null,"cross_file_justification":null,"description":"op_import copies rows from the pending file verbatim after rewriting PEND ids. It never normalizes status, decided_by, decided_by_ref, proposed_by, evidence_sha256 or transitions. A pending file written by a worktree agent can therefore carry rows already marked decided with decided_by operator, and import appends them to the live ledger without passing through confirm. The header comment states that a row reaches decided only through /decisions confirm; import is a second path. Whether validate-artifact.sh catches this cannot be verified because that file was truncated in the diff.","failure_mode":"Rows land in the live ledger as decided by the operator without any operator action, bypassing the confirm gate entirely.","suggested_fix":"In op_import, reject (or rewrite) any row whose status is not open or proposed, force decided_by to null and decided_by_ref to null unless it is a verifiable artifact ref, restrict proposed_by to agent/flatline/dissent, and regenerate the transitions array. Add a bats case covering a pending file that contains a decided row.","anchor_status":"valid","voice":"claude-headless","answered_by":"claude-headless"},{"id":"DISS-C-003","severity":"LOW","category":"input-validation","anchor":".claude/scripts/grimoire-index.sh:emit_decisions","anchor_type":"hunk","anchor_line":177,"anchor_line_end":193,"scope":"diff","trigger_anchor":null,"cross_file_justification":null,"description":"emit_decisions writes agent-authored summary, source and voice text into grimoires/loa/INDEX.md, which the model reads as context. Only control characters are stripped and the length is capped at 160. The id is not restricted to a safe character set before being embedded in the path column. The companion session-start hook in this same change strips angle brackets and backticks and wraps the output in the L6 data fence; the index generator does not, so the same untrusted text reaches the model through a less-guarded channel.","failure_mode":"A summary containing markdown or instruction-like text influences the model when INDEX.md is loaded, undermining the untrusted-content handling the hook applies.","suggested_fix":"Apply the same sanitizer as loa-decisions-surface.sh (replace angle brackets and backticks, restrict id to [A-Za-z0-9-]) and note in the INDEX.md header that decisions rows are untrusted, or fence the decisions section.","anchor_status":"valid","voice":"claude-headless","answered_by":"claude-headless"},{"id":"DISS-C-004","severity":"LOW","category":"input-validation","anchor":".claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh:op_list","anchor_type":"function","anchor_line":660,"anchor_line_end":700,"scope":"cross_file","trigger_anchor":".claude/commands/decisions.md","cross_file_justification":"decisions.md instructs the session to show list --format md output as the preview before every write and to treat rows as untrusted; the writer's md output is the surface where that text enters the operator's session.","description":"The md and tsv formats emit summary, rationale and source with only control characters removed and pipes escaped. No fence or marker separates agent-authored text from the tool's own output, and the md format ends with a fixed prompt to confirm. In the /decisions flow this output is the preview the session reads before acting, so instruction-like text in a rationale sits unmarked next to real tool guidance.","failure_mode":"Agent-authored row text shapes the session's handling of a confirm/reject preview, weakening rule 4 of decisions.md.","suggested_fix":"Wrap row text in the existing L6 data fence from context-isolation-lib.sh when --format md is used, replace angle brackets and backticks as the hook does, and drop the trailing confirm nudge from the tool output.","anchor_status":"valid","voice":"claude-headless","answered_by":"claude-headless"},{"id":"DISS-C-005","severity":"LOW","category":"input-validation","anchor":".claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh:artifact_path","anchor_type":"hunk","anchor_line":291,"anchor_line_end":295,"scope":"diff","trigger_anchor":null,"cross_file_justification":null,"description":"artifact_path resolves only the parent directory with pwd -P and then checks the project-root prefix. A symlink file placed under .flatline/runs or grimoires/loa/a2a that points outside the project passes the containment check, so the recorded evidence_sha256 can refer to a file outside the repository.","failure_mode":"The evidence hash attached to a flatline or dissent voice does not correspond to an in-repo artifact, weakening the audit trail.","suggested_fix":"Resolve the full path including the final component (readlink -f or the compat-lib equivalent) and reject symlinks with a -L test before the prefix check.","anchor_status":"valid","voice":"claude-headless","answered_by":"claude-headless"}],"metadata":{"type":"audit","model":"gpt-5.5-pro","sprint_id":"sprint-1","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:55:53Z","tokens_input":181174,"tokens_output":23857,"cost_usd":0,"latency_ms":74921,"status":"reviewed","degraded":false,"rejected_count":0,"rejected_summary":[],"rejected_sidecar":"grimoires/loa/a2a/sprint-1/adversarial-rejected-audit.jsonl","repaired_count":1,"schema_enforced":false,"parse_path":"normalized","repair_budget_exhausted":0,"repair_skipped_no_hop":0,"repair_wall_seconds":29,"repair_wall_budget_seconds":6000,"repair_hops_skipped":["claude-headless:shared_with_companion"],"model_attempts":["gpt-5.5-pro:reviewed"],"final_model":"gpt-5.5-pro","budget_scale":"diff","budget_cents_effective":423,"budget_cents_max":1200,"companion_voice":{"planned":true,"family":"anthropic","family_basis":"configured_primary","chain":["claude-headless"],"shared_hops":["claude-headless"],"model":"claude-headless","answered_by":"claude-headless","status":"succeeded","failure_class":null,"cost_cents":0,"attempts":["claude-headless:reviewed"],"independent":true,"counted_as":"independent_voice","primary_succeeded_model":"codex-headless","rejected_sidecar":null},"rejected_sidecars":["grimoires/loa/a2a/sprint-1/adversarial-rejected-audit.jsonl"],"hallucination_filter":{"applied":true,"downgraded":0},"scope":{"diff_range":null,"diff_oids":null,"diff_sha256":"bc979beef1d75e3b508293c914bd464031e70f7d6a057f0ee86dd00d7d0bf798","run_tag":null}},"verdict_quality":{"consensus_outcome":"consensus","truncation_waiver_applied":false,"voices_planned":2,"voices_succeeded":2,"voices_succeeded_ids":["codex-headless","claude-headless"],"voices_dropped":[],"chain_health":"ok","confidence_floor":"high","rationale":"multi-voice aggregate (2/2 succeeded); chain_health=ok","single_voice_call":false,"status":"APPROVED"}}
